        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under dry oxygen-free dinitrogen using standard Schlenk techniques, a mixture of H2L (0.178 g, 0.5 mmol) and Ni(OAc)2·4H2O (0.124 g, 0.5 mmol) in MeCN/EtOH (1:3, 20 mL) was stirred and heated under reflux for 10 min. After brief cooling, Eu(OAc)3·4H2O (0.165 g, 0.5 mmol) was added and the mixture was refluxed for 15 min, cooled, and filtered. Slow diffusion of diethyl ether into the filtrate at room temperature afforded blue crystals after two weeks, which were filtered and washed with EtOH (5 mL).",
